<p>Converts a character to an integer value.
</p>
<div class="dascript" style="font-family:monospace; background-color:#F9F9F9; border: 1px dashed #2F6FAB; white-space:pre; line-height:1.25em; padding:1.0em;"><a href="https://github.com/adarec1994/DragonAgeToolset/wiki/Int%20keyword" title="Int keyword">int</a> CharToInt(<br />    <a href="https://github.com/adarec1994/DragonAgeToolset/wiki/String%20keyword" title="String keyword">string</a> sString<br />);</div>
<dl>
<dt>Parameters:
<dd><dl><dt style="font-weight:normal; font-style:italic;">sString<dd>The string character to convert
</dl>
</dl><dl><dt>Returns:
<p><dd>Returns the integer value of the character in the string.
</p>
</dl><dl><dt>Source:
<p><dd><a href="https://github.com/adarec1994/DragonAgeToolset/wiki/Script.ldf" title="Script.ldf">script.ldf</a>
</p>
</dl>
<h2><span class="mw-headline" id="Description">Description</span></h2>
<p>Returns the ascii value of the first character in the string string.
</p>
<h2><span class="mw-headline" id="Remarks">Remarks</span></h2>
<p>If a string with more than one character is passed in, the function will only convert the first character in the string.
</p><p><br />
</p>
